  {
    "number": 184,
    "title": "Restore the remembered scene through MCP",
    "body": "Add `nanoleaf_scene_restore` so an explicit stop request can restore the remembered, still-advertised Lines scene through one existing `scene.activate` command. The animation-options route now returns its opaque `rememberedSceneId`, or null if no valid advertised target is remembered. The tool preserves the caller’s request identity and expected revisions, never changes mode, and returns a typed failure without dispatch when no target exists. Work/Quiet failures explain how to switch to Free.\n\nRefs #150. The shared v1 and extension snapshot shapes stay unchanged. Reading the saved target does not alter the remembered scene or brightness, and the existing worker remains the only light writer. No automatic restoration, installation, personal configuration, live migration or physical operation. Two capability specs are synchronized and the issue-linked change is archived.\n\nValidation: focused Python and MCP red/green tests; post-adoption full Python 611 tests and MCP 86 tests with immutable package verification/build/typecheck; full browser suite; workflow 10 tests, 21 specs and 41 complete archives. Controller tests cover remembered/missing/deleted scenes and pure reads. MCP tests cover exact one-command delegation, null and malformed options, scope revocation, Free gating, replay and uncertainty, with both protocol versions.\n\nFrozen comparison: base/merge-base `9e25a4c9cde3f81e9186aefcddb364f9060e5301`, head `0995c000b74635f0b0f996bf276627d5c7d4ea36`; `git diff 9e25a4c9cde3f81e9186aefcddb364f9060e5301...0995c000b74635f0b0f996bf276627d5c7d4ea36`. Worktree clean. The squash-base refresh preserved both base and candidate trees. Independent Standards and Specification reviews, all five exact-head Depot jobs and prior main CI remain merge gates. Owner-approved CI evidence uses repository check records and annotations for sign-in-only Depot result pages.\n",
    "state": "open",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/jimmie-potts/codex-nanoleaf/pull/184",
